# Editor / OS junk
*~
*#
*.swp
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
dist-client/

# Test / lint caches
.coverage
.coverage.*
.cache/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.hypothesis/
htmlcov/
# JUnit XML written by CI's `--junitxml=reports/…` steps (.github/workflows/ci.yml,
# full.yml). Ignored so copying a CI invocation locally cannot leave a report a
# `git add -A` would sweep into a commit.
/reports/

# Virtualenvs (lives at the repo root: .venv/)
venv/
.venv/
.venv-client/

# Linked git worktrees (`git worktree add .worktrees/<name>`). GLOB-anchored at the root
# because each entry is an EMBEDDED GIT REPOSITORY: `git add -A` stages it as a gitlink
# pointing at a local absolute path that exists on no other machine, and git says so
# itself — "Clones of the outer repository will not contain the contents of the embedded
# repository and will not know how to obtain it." So the artefact of the single most
# ordinary contributor reflex is a broken clone for every user of a PUBLIC repo. Ignored
# rather than documented-around, because the reflex is what has to be safe (#3413).
/.worktrees/

# Per-user local tool state (`gh` writes .local/state/gh/device-id — a stable installation
# identifier). Nothing under here is repo content and none of it is reproducible on another
# machine; it exists only because XDG-style tools default to the nearest writable root.
/.local/

# IDE / editor configs
.vscode/
.idea/
*.sublime-*
*.iml
*.code-workspace
pyrightconfig.json

# Environment / secrets (.env.example stays tracked)
.env
.env.local

# Frontend
node_modules/
web/dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
# Workspace members must NOT carry their own lockfiles — the root package-lock.json
# is the single source of truth for the npm workspace (web, desktop). Stray member
# lockfiles trip npm's optional-dependency bug (npm/cli#4828) → broken native builds.
web/package-lock.json
desktop/package-lock.json
web/test-results/
web/playwright-report/
# The e2e harness's authenticated cookie jar — holds a LIVE gateway token.
web/e2e/.auth/

# Static assets generated from frontend build (tracked as a symlink is fine;
# a real directory here would be a stale copy — see docs on web build/serve)
src/personalclaw/static/dist

# Desktop app build artifacts (Electron + bundled PyInstaller backend)
desktop/dist/
desktop/out/
desktop/backend-dist/
*.dmg

# Local dev / runtime state
.personalclaw-dev*/
.mcp.json
runs.json
TASK_PROGRESS.md
dev-seed.sh
# Dev-session screenshots dropped at repo root (the app icon lives in desktop/)
/*.png

# Eval harness output
eval_results/

# Local tooling
.claude/
.playwright-mcp/
playwright-responses/

# Bare local dev gateway home (make serve creates $(CURDIR)/.dev-home).
# GLOB, not a fixed name: every dev home holds live credentials (.local_secret,
# session_key, sel_hmac.key), so an ad-hoc `.dev-home-<something>` for a one-off
# validation run must be ignored by default rather than each name being added
# after the fact. A `git add -A` in a repo root with an unignored dev home stages
# secrets — do not narrow this back to an exact match.
/.dev-home*/
# e2e harness dev home (playwright.config.ts recipe)
/.dev-home-e2e/
# Seeded marketing-screenshot home (the release runbook clones .dev-home into this).
# It holds a real signing key, live session records and credential material, so it must
# never be committable — the same reason .dev-home is ignored.
/.screenshot-home/

# Owner-provided local secrets — never committed. The real file lives at the
# workspace root (outside every repo); this rule is belt-and-braces.
.secrets.env

# SQLite sidecars beside the COMMITTED test fixtures. The fixture homes ship real `.db`
# files, and every store opens with `PRAGMA journal_mode=WAL`, so merely booting a gateway
# or opening one of those databases in place drops a `-wal`/`-shm` next to it. Those are
# runtime residue, never fixture content: the generator folds the WAL back in with
# `PRAGMA wal_checkpoint(TRUNCATE)` (scripts/generate_six_month_home_fixture.py::_checkpoint)
# precisely so the committed `.db` is self-contained. Ignored because a `git add -A` that
# swept them in would pin a half-checkpointed fixture — the silent-emptying the six-month
# home exists to catch. If a fixture ever looks EMPTY, re-run the generator; do not commit
# a sidecar to carry the missing rows.
src/personalclaw/tests_fixtures/**/*.db-wal
src/personalclaw/tests_fixtures/**/*.db-shm

# Outstanding mutation session (scripts/mutation_harness.py): pristine copies of the
# files a mutation run is holding, plus its journal. Ignored so the residue-detection
# directory never becomes a staged file — but NOT ignored by the rail: `pre-commit`
# tests for the directory itself and refuses the commit, so an ignored residue is a
# LOUD residue rather than a hidden one.
/.mutation-session/

# Per-worktree pytest bootstrap. A linked worktree has no venv of its own, and an editable
# install in the main checkout means a bare `import personalclaw` from a worktree resolves to
# the MAIN checkout's src — so a lane writes a small runner that strips the editable finder
# and re-points sys.path before collecting. It is scaffolding for one session, never repo
# content, and `git add -A` would sweep it in (it did, once, during this rule's own change).
/.lane_pytest.py
